# bmcd is a cargo package: Buildroot fetches the GitHub archive, runs
# `cargo vendor`, and stores the re-packed archive (the "-cargo2" suffix)
# -- so the sum covers the vendored crates too, exactly as Buildroot does
# for its own cargo packages.
#
# THE SUM DEPENDS ON THE RUST TOOLCHAIN, not just on the commit. The
# archive is named after the commit alone, so a stale one in dl/ looks
# right and hashes wrong. Measured on 2026-09-08 against commit 9b5cffa:
# rust-bin 1.85.0 vendored
# 9815f9cb190773112439b8979222f45ee79124f15ace2d29c5484141be679f65,
# rust-bin 1.98.1 vendored
# 84b9825371b085cea0f21ef03efd50893cfb16c0806cecb98c3700d605b44b9c.
# Recompute after any Rust bump, from a tree re-extracted AFTER the bump --
# buildroot_patches/ are applied at extract time, so a tree extracted
# before the patch changed still carries the old toolchain and produces the
# old sum under a name that looks correct.
#
# Computed with buildroot/local.mk REMOVED. A dev override rsyncs a working
# tree instead of downloading the pinned archive, so a hash computed with one
# in place would describe whatever happened to be on the workstation.
#
# The version is commit e7c1d90 on excavador-turing/bmcd branch `hive`,
# released as v2.33.0: a node's USB bus number is not part of its identity.
#
# The port check that stops a flash of node 2 writing node 1 compared the whole
# path, bus included, against a bus hardcoded to 1. This board pairs an OHCI
# and an EHCI controller as COMPANIONS for the same physical ports, so which
# bus a device lands on is decided by its speed -- the same hub port is 1-1.2
# for a full-speed device and 2-1.2 for a high-speed one. A Rockchip in maskrom
# is high-speed, so the check refused every RK1 it was ever asked to flash:
#
#   node 2 requested on 1-1.2; found Rockusb on 2-1.2 instead
#
# Found on bmc-2 on 2026-09-11 while recovering a node that would not boot; the
# module was healthy and our own check was the only thing in the way. Nothing
# on this board could be flashed or exposed as mass storage through the daemon
# until this release.
#
# No listener change, no gate change, no new setting.
#
# Measured 2026-09-11 with rust-bin 1.98.1 in the pinned container, from a
# tree with no buildroot/local.mk: `make bmcd-source` reported got
# 379d140d against a zeroed expectation, then re-run to confirm it fetches
# and verifies cleanly.
